Weather, remote access and short construction seasons in Alberta all raise the stakes. That means naming one accountable person and a clear decision date. Regulators and Indigenous partners expect early, honest engagement, and projects go smoother when they get it. The first step is agreeing what a good outcome looks like before the design is frozen. Our teams have seen the same pattern across several Oil and Gas sites: small gaps early become schedule slips later. Field crews should be involved before drawings are issued for construction, not after.

